# What Docker must not even be handed, let alone copy in.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs `app`, so none of this reaches the image today. The
# build *context* is a different matter: everything not listed here is sent to
# the daemon before the first instruction runs, which on this repo means a
# hundred megabytes of client drawing sets on every build. It is also one
# careless `COPY . .` away from putting them, and the .env, inside the image.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Client drawings and anything derived from them.
test/
corpus/
bakeoff/
*.pdf
*_detect*.json
*_results.json
Door detection- *.html

.git/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
